  {
   "parameters": {
    "content": "## Booking Guard 2: YES / NO / CANCEL reply handling\nPoint your Twilio number's incoming-message webhook here. YES = water, power, keys and parking are ready (booking becomes Confirmed). NO = something is missing: the row is marked and you are alerted to call. CANCEL cancels and applies your notice rule to the deposit (inside the notice window it is forfeited, outside it is marked refund due). Anything else is forwarded to you.\n\n**Setup**\n1. In Twilio, set your number's \"A message comes in\" webhook (HTTP POST) to this workflow's Production URL.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with tabs Bookings and Report using the CSV headers in the sheet-templates folder; paste its ID into the Config node (sheetId).\n3. Fill in the Config node: business name, owner email, time zone offset (for example -05:00), channel (sms or email), deposit amount and your own Stripe/PayPal payment link, notice hours.\n4. Attach credentials on nodes with a warning icon: Google Sheets OAuth2, SMTP, and Twilio (HTTP Basic Auth: Account SID / Auth Token) if you use SMS.\n5. Execute once with test rows, then activate.",
